<div class="sheet-area flex-columns">

	<div class="sheet-headline sheet-banner splatFont">
		<span class="sheet-banner-text">{{localize 'wod.spheres.spheres'}}</span>
	</div>

	<div class="">
		{{#each spheres as |sphere index|}}

			{{#if (eq (mod index 3) 0)}}<div class="magic-statArea pullLeft">{{/if}}

			<div class="sphere-itemlist">
				<div class="headlineNormal sphere-itemlist {{#if (eq sphere.system.id ../actor.system.bio.splatfields.affinity.value)}}highlightedPowerRow{{/if}}" style="width: 100%;">
					{{!-- THE DESCRIPTION EYE IS HERE, IN THE NAME CELL, AND DELIBERATELY NOT IN THE
					      iconBox BELOW. This comment replaces the "NO description eye here" one that
					      stood in this file from 7.5.6 to 7.5.29. It was right, and it recorded two
					      MEASURED objections; both have since been answered, each by a different change,
					      and neither answer was available when it was written:

					      1. "0 of 243 live Sphere items carry a description, so the eye renders DISABLED
					         on every row." Answered by add-sphere-descriptions (the DATA half, in
					         `webgen/`): the description no longer comes from the actor's Sphere item at
					         all — which is still empty, because the system creates those items itself.
					         Nine `sphere` documents, each carrying the Sphere's rank 1..5 ladder derived
					         from its five `sphere-effect` records, ship in the `mage-spheres` compendium
					         pack, and the eye opens THAT document read-only (`item-viewer.js`), matched
					         on `sphere.system.id` by `trait-enrichment.js`. The eye is rendered only
					         where that match was found at render time (`sphereCompendiumUuid`, built in
					         `preparePowersContext`), so while the pack is absent this block looks
					         EXACTLY as it did before — fewer eyes, never a dead one.

					      2. "Un-gating the iconBox from `locked` made a locked sheet render an icon box
					         that had never been there, which took the width the fifth dot needs, so the
					         fifth dot wrapped onto its own line under every column." Answered by 7.5.16's
					         `wod-namecell` (written for the Attributes block, which broke in precisely
					         this way, and written to be reused here). The iconBox and its `locked` gate
					         below are UNTOUCHED: the eye is inside the name cell, which already carries
					         this row's width (`spheres-headlineWidth`, 55% on a PC sheet), and the label
					         beside it has `min-width: 0`, so the cell cannot grow and the dots keep every
					         pixel they had. That is also why the eye can render on a LOCKED sheet — it is
					         a read affordance, and it no longer depends on the gate that made 7.5.5's
					         attempt change a locked sheet's layout.

					      The eye is a SIBLING of the label, never a child: ApplicationV2 dispatches a
					      click to the nearest [data-action] ancestor, so an eye nested inside a rollable
					      label would roll dice instead of opening the description. Keep `collapsible
					      button` on it — the binder selects `.collapsible.button[data-traituuid]`, and
					      `.icon.collapsible.button` is also what caps the icon's height. --}}
					<div class="spheres-headlineWidth wod-namecell">
						{{#if (lookup ../sphereCompendiumUuid sphere.system.id)}}
							<i class="pointer icon collapsible button fa-solid fa-eye wod-namecell-eye"
								title="{{localize 'wod.labels.show.description'}}"
								data-traituuid="{{lookup ../sphereCompendiumUuid sphere.system.id}}"></i>
						{{/if}}
						{{!-- The label is clipped to one line in this block (css/mage.css), because the
						      eye's 22px is enough to wrap the longest TECHNOCRATIC names onto a second
						      line inside a 26px row. So the non-affinity rows now carry their own name
						      as a `title`: the tail of a clipped name stays one hover away, exactly as
						      7.5.27 did for long Feature names. The affinity row keeps the title it has
						      always had — its name ("Fuerzas", "Vida", …) is never the clipped one. --}}
						{{!-- cast-from-sphere-name: the label already carried `vrollable` but no
						      action, so clicking it did nothing. It now opens the spell-casting
						      dialog with THIS sphere pre-selected at the character's rank — see the
						      `castsphere` branch in action-helpers.js. --}}
						<div class="headlineNormalSpheres splatFont vrollable wod-namecell-label"
							data-action="rollDice"
							data-castsphere="true"
							data-key="{{sphere.system.id}}"
							data-value="{{sphere.system.value}}"
							{{#if (eq sphere.system.id ../actor.system.bio.splatfields.affinity.value)}}
								title="{{localize 'wod.bio.mage.affinitysphere'}}"
							{{else}}
								title="{{localize sphere.system.label}}"
							{{/if}}>
							{{localize sphere.system.label}}
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="resource-value" 
						data-itemid="{{sphere._id}}"
						data-key="{{sphere.system.id}}"
						data-value="{{sphere.system.value}}" 
						data-name="system.value">

						{{#numLoop sphere.system.max}}					
							<span class="{{#if (gt sphere.system.max 5)}}supernaturalAttribute{{/if}} resource-value-step" data-action="editDot" data-type="{{../../config.sheettype.mage}}" data-index="{{this}}" data-itemid="{{sphere._id}}" data-ability="core"></span>					
						{{/numLoop}}						
						
					</div>
					{{!-- Still NO eye in this iconBox, and `showtooltip` is still not passed to
					      list_icons.hbs — see the long comment on the name cell above for why the eye
					      moved there instead. Nothing about this gate changes: the pencil-edit icon
					      stays unlocked-only, and the width this box takes is the width it always
					      took. --}}
					{{#if (eq ../locked false)}}
						<div class="iconBox">
							{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/list_icons.hbs" showedit=true item=sphere locked=../locked edittitle="wod.labels.edit.sphere" collapseclass="power"}}
						</div>
					{{else}}
						{{#if (gte sphere.system.value 4)}}
							<div class="pullRight speciality-magic-icon">
								<i class="fa-solid fa-circle-exclamation {{#if (eq sphere.system.speciality '')}}item-warning{{else}}item-notice{{/if}}" data-tooltip="{{#if (eq sphere.system.speciality '')}}{{localize 'wod.labels.ability.specialitynone'}}{{else}}{{localize 'wod.labels.ability.speciality'}}: {{sphere.system.speciality}}{{/if}}"></i>
							</div>
						{{else}}
							<div class="pullRight speciality-magic-empty-icon">
								&nbsp;
							</div>
						{{/if}}
					{{/if}}
				</div>

			</div>
			{{!-- No inline .description panel here, and none is coming back:
			      open-item-window-from-eye-icon removed it, and it had always been dead code in this
			      file anyway (nothing ever rendered an eye here to toggle it). The eye above opens a
			      window instead — a compendium document, not this item. --}}

			{{#if (eq (mod index 3) 2)}}</div>{{/if}}
		
		{{/each}}	
	</div> 

</div>